.TH MDOWSER 1 "2026" "MDowser" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdowser \- browse text/markdown over HTTPS and local files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdowser
.RI [ file | url ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdowser
is a native desktop browser for the plain-text web. Each argument is opened
as a document, in its own tab: either an
.B https://
URL or a local path (an absolute path, a
.B file://
URL or a
.B ~
-relative path; a bare path gets a
.B .md
completion attempt).
.PP
Documents are fetched with a single
.B GET
over HTTPS (there is no
.B http://
support) or read from the local filesystem, parsed once as CommonMark with
GFM-style extensions, and
rendered with a desktop-browser-style interface. There is no webview, no
JavaScript, no cookies and no proxy. Repeat visits use a bounded, encrypted
on-disk HTTP cache, which the app clears or disables from its preferences.
Being a GUI application it has only the two options listed under OPTIONS
below; every other argument is an open target.
.PP
When the application is already running, a new launch opens its targets in a
new instance; MDowser does not use a single-instance guard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print the usage synopsis on standard output and exit without opening a
window.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version on standard output and exit without opening a window.
.PP
Every other argument is an open target; words that begin with a hyphen are
ignored, so a macOS Finder launch's
.B \-psn_
argument is never treated as a document. On Windows the windowed subsystem
has no console: the flags are no-ops there and the
.IR .exe
properties carry the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the encrypted settings, session, history, bookmarks and
cache.
Defaults to
.IR $HOME/.local/share ;
MDowser uses the
.I mdowser
subdirectory. A relative value is ignored (the specification requires an
absolute path).
.TP
.B HOME
Used to derive the default data directory when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset or relative.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/mdowser/
Encrypted per-user data: preferences, session, history, bookmarks, the HTTP
cache and the single shared key file. Apart from a document the user
explicitly saves with
.B Ctrl/Cmd+S
(which goes to the downloads folder), nothing is written outside this
directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR rpm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
MDowser. Full documentation:
.IR README.md ,
.IR docs/BUILDING.md .
.PP
Homepage: https://github.com/MDowser/MDowser
